---@field reply_mode anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSettingSource|distilled.Null The settings level `reply_mode` comes from: the channel when it stores one. With `include_inherited=true` and no stored mode it is `default`.

---Every settings level that contributes text to `instructions`, broadest first, in the order their text is joined. Empty when none does.
---@alias anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSettingSourcesInstructionsList anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSettingSource[]

---Claude Tag settings. Without `include_inherited`, a setting that is null is not set on the settings level and is inherited. With it, `enabled` and `guest_policy` are never null, `instructions`, `model` and `environment_id` are null when no settings level sets them, and `reply_mode` is null unless the channel itself stores one.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSettings
---@field enabled boolean|distilled.Null Whether Claude is on. The nearest settings level that sets it decides.
---@field instructions string|distilled.Null Instructions for Claude. Instructions add up: the text of every settings level that sets it is joined, broadest first.
---@field model string|distilled.Null The model Claude uses: a model identifier or the name of a model line. The nearest settings level that sets it decides. When none does, Claude uses the product's default model.
---@field environment_id string|distilled.Null The environment Claude's sessions run in, starting with `env_`, or the identifier of a self-hosted runner pool, starting with `ccpool_`. The nearest settings level that sets it decides.
---@field guest_policy anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagGuestPolicy|distilled.Null What Claude does in a channel while a Slack guest is in it. The nearest settings level that sets it decides.
---@field reply_mode anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagReplyMode|distilled.Null How Claude takes part in the channel. Only a channel stores one, and no settings level passes one on, so it is always null on a workspace. Null on a channel means the channel stores none yet: Claude then follows the reply mode chosen in Slack, if one was, else `automatic`. A stored reply mode can be changed but never cleared.

---The settings in a request that sets a Slack channel up. A setting left out is not set. A setting sent as null is cleared.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSettingsCreate
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Whether Claude is on. `true` on a channel turns Claude on in it even when its workspace stores `false`. Null clears it.
---@field instructions? string|distilled.Null Instructions for Claude, up to 8,192 characters after leading and trailing white space is trimmed. Null or blank text clears them.
---@field model? string|distilled.Null The model Claude uses: the identifier of a model, or the name of a model line, that the organization is entitled to for Claude Tag. Null clears it.
---@field environment_id? string|distilled.Null The environment Claude's sessions run in: the identifier of an active environment of the organization, starting with `env_`, or of a self-hosted runner pool of the organization that every member may use, starting with `ccpool_`. Null clears it.
---@field guest_policy? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagGuestPolicy|distilled.Null What Claude does in a channel while a Slack guest is in it. Null clears it.
---@field reply_mode? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagReplyMode|distilled.Null How Claude takes part in the channel: `automatic`, `mention_only`, `always_awake` or `thread`. Only a channel takes one: an update of a workspace that sends a value is refused, and one that sends null changes nothing. Null never clears it: sent to a channel that stores none it changes nothing, and sent to a channel that stores one it is refused, because a stored reply mode can be changed but never cleared; a caller that wants Claude's default behavior sends `automatic`.

---The settings to change. A setting left out is unchanged. A setting sent as null is cleared, so it is inherited.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSettingsUpdate
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Whether Claude is on. `true` on a channel turns Claude on in it even when its workspace stores `false`. Null clears it.
---@field instructions? string|distilled.Null Instructions for Claude, up to 8,192 characters after leading and trailing white space is trimmed. Null or blank text clears them.
---@field model? string|distilled.Null The model Claude uses: the identifier of a model, or the name of a model line, that the organization is entitled to for Claude Tag. Null clears it.
---@field environment_id? string|distilled.Null The environment Claude's sessions run in: the identifier of an active environment of the organization, starting with `env_`, or of a self-hosted runner pool of the organization that every member may use, starting with `ccpool_`. Null clears it.
---@field guest_policy? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagGuestPolicy|distilled.Null What Claude does in a channel while a Slack guest is in it. Null clears it.
---@field reply_mode? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagReplyMode|distilled.Null How Claude takes part in the channel: `automatic`, `mention_only`, `always_awake` or `thread`. Only a channel takes one: an update of a workspace that sends a value is refused, and one that sends null changes nothing. Null never clears it: sent to a channel that stores none it changes nothing, and sent to a channel that stores one it is refused, because a stored reply mode can be changed but never cleared; a caller that wants Claude's default behavior sends `automatic`.

---A Slack channel set up for Claude Tag, with the settings it stores or, with `include_inherited`, the settings that apply in it.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSlackChannel
---@field type string
---@field id string The channel's identifier. Starts with `slch_`. It does not change for as long as the channel is set up, with one exception: a channel that is not configured can get a new one. A channel that is removed and set up again also has a new one. The old one keeps returning 404; look the channel up by its Slack identifiers for the new one.
---@field slack anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSlackChannelIdentifiers Slack's own identifiers for the channel.
---@field settings anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSettings What the channel itself stores or, with `include_inherited`, what applies in it. `sources` says which.
---@field sources anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaClaudeTagSettingSources For each setting, the settings level its value in `settings` comes from.
---@field created_at string Time the channel was set up, by whichever route. It does not change for as long as `id` does not.
---@field updated_at string Time Claude Tag's record of the channel last changed. It moves on every change to a setting, and can also move when something no response holds changes, so a later value says to read the channel again, not that a setting changed. Attaching or detaching a Bundle does not by itself move it.

