---@field service_tier anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaUsageReportServiceTier|distilled.Null Service tier used. `null` if not grouping by service tier.
---@field context_window anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaMessagesUsageReportContextWindow|distilled.Null Context window used. `null` if not grouping by context window. A request is classified by comparing its prompt size with its model's own long-context boundary, the same boundary that billing uses. The two values are labels for the two classes, not literal ranges: where a model's boundary is below 200k, a request whose prompt exceeds that boundary is reported under `200k-1M`, and a `0-200k` filter does not return it. Where the report cannot determine a model's boundary, it uses 200k instead. Usage stored before this classification took effect may still be reported under its earlier value, at any `bucket_width`, until it expires. Billed amounts are not affected.
---@field inference_geo anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaInferenceGeoFilter|distilled.Null Inference geo used matching requests' `inference_geo` parameter if set, otherwise the workspace's `default_inference_geo`. For models that do not support specifying `inference_geo` the value is `"not_available"`. Always `null` if not grouping by inference geo.
