---An OpenTelemetry destination: an OTLP/HTTP endpoint, the request headers sent with every delivery to it, what the exported spans contain, and which workspaces it covers. A destination belongs to an organization. A workspace's spans go to every enabled destination that covers it.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestination
---@field type string
---@field id string The unique ID of the destination (`tdst_...`).
---@field display_name string|distilled.Null Human-readable name for the destination. Null when none was set.
---@field endpoint_url string The base URL of the destination's OTLP/HTTP endpoint, exactly as registered. The API appends the per-signal path, such as `/v1/traces`, on delivery, unless `traces.endpoint_url` is set.
---@field header_names anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationHeaderNamesList Names of the registered request headers. Header values are write-only and are never returned.
---@field traces anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTraces The destination's settings for the traces it receives.
---@field state anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationState Whether the destination receives deliveries.
---@field delivery_health anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDeliveryHealth The most recent delivery results for this destination.
---@field created_at string Time the destination was created.
---@field updated_at string Time of the last change to the destination's configuration or state. Changes to `delivery_health` don't change it. An update that sets a header value always changes it, even when the value is the same as before. Adding or removing a single workspace on the destination's list doesn't change it. An update that changes the list does.
---@field workspaces anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationWorkspaces Which of the organization's workspaces the destination covers.

---What the spans that the API exports to a telemetry destination contain.
---
---See the [OpenTelemetry export guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/opentelemetry#choose-a-content-mode) to learn what the spans contain in each content mode.
---@alias anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationContentMode "metadata_only"|"content"

---The most recent delivery results that the API records for a telemetry destination.
---
---Changes to the destination's configuration or state don't reset these fields. Changes to these fields don't change `updated_at`. The values can lag behind the latest deliveries.
---
---See the [OpenTelemetry export guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/opentelemetry#delivery-and-health) to learn how the API delivers spans and when it disables a destination.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDeliveryHealth
---@field last_success_at string|distilled.Null Time of the most recent successful delivery to the destination, or `null` if no delivery has succeeded yet.
---@field last_error string|distilled.Null A message that describes the most recent failed delivery to the destination, or `null` if no delivery has failed yet. Examples are `temporary DNS failure`, `TLS failure`, `timeout`, `connection failure`, `invalid address`, `HTTP error (status 503)`, and `redirect (status 301)`. The message is `invalid address` both for a hostname that doesn't exist and for an address that isn't publicly routable. It never contains the endpoint's response body, a header value, a network address, or TLS details. `last_error` and `last_error_at` always change together. A later successful delivery doesn't clear them. If `last_success_at` is later than `last_error_at`, a delivery has succeeded since this failure. See the [OpenTelemetry export guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/opentelemetry#delivery-errors) to learn the likely cause of each error.
---@field last_error_at string|distilled.Null Time of the failure that `last_error` describes. Changes together with `last_error`. Null until a delivery first fails.

---Why the destination is disabled: `caller` when a caller disabled it, or the reason the API disabled it automatically (`sustained_failure`, `invalid_address`, or `redirect`). Every automatic disable is reversible with an update that sets `state` to `enabled`. An update that sets `disabled` on a destination that is already disabled keeps its reason.
---@alias anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReason anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReasonCaller|anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReasonSustainedFailure|anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReasonInvalidAddress|anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReasonRedirect

---A caller disabled the destination with an update that set `state` to `disabled`.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReasonCaller
---@field type string

---The API disabled the destination because deliveries to it failed for longer than the same threshold as for `sustained_failure`, and the most recent failed delivery failed with an invalid address: the DNS answer says that the endpoint's hostname doesn't exist or doesn't have an address, or the address that the API would connect to isn't publicly routable or is reserved, for example a loopback, link-local, private-network, or cloud-metadata address. The API doesn't connect to such an address, and retries the delivery a bounded number of times as it does after a timeout. A timeout or a server failure of the DNS lookup is a temporary DNS failure instead, not an invalid address.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReasonInvalidAddress
---@field type string

---The API disabled the destination because the endpoint answered a delivery with a 3xx status. Redirects are never followed, and one such answer disables the destination at once.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReasonRedirect
---@field type string

---The API disabled the destination because deliveries to it failed, with no successful delivery in between, for longer than a threshold that Anthropic configures and that is not part of this contract. The reason is `invalid_address` instead when the most recent failed delivery failed with an invalid address.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReasonSustainedFailure
---@field type string

---Names of the registered request headers. Header values are write-only and are never returned.
---@alias anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationHeaderNamesList string[]

---Whether a telemetry destination receives deliveries.
---
---A caller can set either state. The API also disables an enabled destination on its own in some cases. The `reason` of the disabled state says whether a caller or the API disabled the destination and, when the API did, why.
---
---See the [OpenTelemetry export guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/opentelemetry#delivery-and-health) to learn when the API disables a destination.
---@alias anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationState anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateEnabled|anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateDisabled

---The API doesn't deliver anything to the telemetry destination.
---
---Spans produced while it is disabled aren't delivered later.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateDisabled
---@field type string
---@field reason anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationDisabledReason Whether a caller or the API disabled the destination and, when the API did, why. Read-only.

---Stop deliveries to the telemetry destination.
---
---Spans produced while it is disabled aren't delivered later. A destination that is already disabled keeps its `reason`.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateDisabledParams
---@field type string

---The telemetry destination receives the spans of the workspaces that it covers.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateEnabled
---@field type string

---Start deliveries to the telemetry destination again.
---
---This doesn't reset `delivery_health`.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateEnabledParams
---@field type string

---The state to set on a telemetry destination, by `type` alone.
---
---A caller can't set the `reason` of a disabled state. Only the API sets it.
---@alias anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateParams anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateEnabledParams|anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationStateDisabledParams

---The result of one test span sent to a destination.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTest
---@field type string
---@field result anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTestResult How the test went: `success` when the destination answered with a 2xx status, else `failure` with the reason.

---The test span was not delivered.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTestFailure
---@field type string
---@field error string A message that describes why the test span was not delivered, including the HTTP status code when the destination returned one. Examples: `HTTP error (status 403)`, `timeout`, `TLS failure`. It has the same form as the destination's `delivery_health.last_error` and never contains the destination's response body, any header value, a network address, or TLS details.

---The outcome of a test: `success`, or `failure` with the reason.
---@alias anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTestResult anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTestSuccess|anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTestFailure

---The destination answered the test span with a 2xx status.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTestSuccess
---@field type string

---A telemetry destination's settings for the traces it receives.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTraces
---@field enabled boolean Whether the destination receives traces. A destination whose `enabled` is false keeps its other settings.
---@field endpoint_url string|distilled.Null The full URL that the API posts traces to, exactly as registered, or `null` if the destination doesn't have one. When it is `null`, the API posts traces to `endpoint_url` with `/v1/traces` appended.
---@field content_mode anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationContentMode What the exported spans contain.
---@field max_content_bytes number|distilled.Null The most bytes of content that one exported span can contain, or `null` if only the API's maximum applies. Content means model prompts and responses, and tool inputs and outputs. The API shortens longer content to this size before it delivers the span. A destination whose `content_mode` is `metadata_only` keeps this value. It applies once `content_mode` is `content`.

---The settings for the traces that a telemetry destination receives, as a create or update request sets them. An omitted field takes its default on create and keeps its stored value on update.
---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTracesParams
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the destination receives traces. Defaults to true on create. It cannot be null.
---@field endpoint_url? string|distilled.Null The full URL of your collector's traces endpoint, for a collector that takes traces on a path other than `/v1/traces`. The API posts traces to it exactly as given and appends nothing. The same rules as for `endpoint_url` apply, except that any path is allowed. It must have the same scheme, host, and port as `endpoint_url`. At most 2,048 characters. On create, `null` is the same as leaving it out. On update, `null` removes it. The API then posts traces to `endpoint_url` with `/v1/traces` appended. A change of this URL alone keeps the registered headers.
---@field content_mode? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationContentMode|string|distilled.Null What the exported spans contain. Defaults to `metadata_only` on create. On update, `null` sets `metadata_only`.
---@field max_content_bytes? number|distilled.Null The most bytes of content that one exported span can contain, from 1 up to the API's maximum. `null` sets no bound, so only the API's maximum applies. On create, leaving it out is the same as `null`. The error for a value above the maximum states the maximum.

---A workspace on a telemetry destination's workspace list.
