---@class anthropic.beta_organizations.CreateTelemetryDestinationRequest
---@field anthropicVersion? string The version of the Claude API you want to use. Read more about versioning and our version history [here](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/versioning).
---@field anthropicBeta? anthropic.beta_organizations.CreateTelemetryDestinationRequestAnthropicBetaList This endpoint is in beta: requests must send `telemetry-destinations-2026-08-11` in this header.
---@field display_name? string|distilled.Null Human-readable name for the destination. Optional. 1 to 255 characters.
---@field endpoint_url string The base URL of your collector's OTLP/HTTP endpoint, for example `https://gateway.example.com`. The URL must use `https` and a hostname, not an IP address. The port, if given, must be 443. The URL must not contain a query string, a fragment, or a username and password. At most 2,048 characters. A path prefix, such as `/otlp`, is allowed. Don't include the per-signal path (`/v1/traces`), because the API appends it on delivery. If your collector takes traces on another path, also set `traces.endpoint_url`.
---@field headers? anthropic.beta_organizations.CreateTelemetryDestinationRequestHeadersMap Request headers that the API sends with every delivery, typically your collector's authentication header (for example `authorization`). The API never returns the values. Reads show only `header_names`. At most 20 headers. Names are at most 128 characters. Two names can't differ only in case. Values are printable ASCII, at most 4,096 characters, and can't begin or end with a space. Names and values together are at most 16,384 bytes. Reserved names are rejected, for example `host`, `cookie`, `user-agent`, and names that start with `content-`, `proxy-`, `x-forwarded-`, or `anthropic-`. For this check, `_` in a name counts as `-`.
---@field traces? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationTracesParams The settings for the traces that the destination receives. If you leave it out, every setting takes its default.
---@field workspaces anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationWorkspacesParams Which of the organization's workspaces the destination covers.

---This endpoint is in beta: requests must send `telemetry-destinations-2026-08-11` in this header.
---@alias anthropic.beta_organizations.CreateTelemetryDestinationRequestAnthropicBetaList anthropic.beta_organizations.AnthropicBeta[]

