---@field workspace_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestWorkspaceIdsList Filter to usage in specific workspaces, by tagged workspace ID (`wrkspc_...`). Use `group_by[]=workspace_id` to break out per-workspace values. Claude Platform organizations only; matches nothing for a Claude Enterprise organization.
---@field service_tiers__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestServiceTiersList Filter to specific service tiers. Use `group_by[]=service_tier` to break out per-tier values. Claude Platform organizations only; matches nothing for a Claude Enterprise organization.
---@field rbac_group_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestRbacGroupIdsList Filter to usage attributed to specific RBAC groups. Accepts tagged RBAC group IDs (`rbac_group_...`) or bare group UUIDs. A row matches when the user belonged to any of the listed groups on the (UTC) day the usage occurred; usage with no group attribution never matches.
---@field user_profile_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestUserProfileIdsList Filter to usage attributed to specific user profiles, by tagged user profile ID (`uprof_...`). Use `group_by[]=user_profile_id` to break out per-profile values. Claude Platform organizations only.
---@field agent_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestAgentIdsList Filter to usage incurred by sessions of specific Claude Managed Agents agents. Use `group_by[]=agent_id` to break out per-agent values. Claude Platform organizations only.
---@field environment_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestEnvironmentIdsList Filter to usage incurred by Claude Managed Agents sessions that ran in specific environments. Use `group_by[]=environment_id` to break out per-environment values. Claude Platform organizations only.
---@field deployment_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestDeploymentIdsList Filter to usage incurred by Claude Managed Agents sessions that specific deployments started. Use `group_by[]=deployment_id` to break out per-deployment values. Claude Platform organizations only.
---@field session_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestSessionIdsList Filter to usage incurred by specific Claude Managed Agents sessions, by tagged session ID (`sesn_...`). Use `group_by[]=session_id` to break out per-session values. Claude Platform organizations only.
---@field actor_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestActorIdsList Filter to usage attributed to specific identities, by tagged ID: a `user_...`, `svac_...` (service account), or `apikey_...` ID. An `apikey_` entry matches only usage attributed to the key itself, not usage on that key attributed to a user or service account (use `api_key_ids[]` for every request a key authenticated). Federated identities have no tagged ID; select them with `actor_types[]`. Use `group_by[]=actor` to break out per-identity values.
---@field actor_types__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestActorTypesList Filter to usage attributed to specific kinds of identity. Use `group_by[]=actor_type` to break out per-kind values.
---@field api_key_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestApiKeyIdsList Filter to usage authenticated by specific API keys, by tagged API key ID (`apikey_...`), whichever identity the usage is attributed to. Include an empty entry (`api_key_ids[]=`) to also match usage that no API key authenticated. Use `group_by[]=api_key_id` to break out per-key values; usage without a key has a null `api_key_id`. Claude Platform organizations only.
---@field organization_ids__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestOrganizationIdsList Filter a parent organization's report to specific child organizations, by organization UUID or `org_` ID; an ID that is not one of its child organizations matches nothing. Requires an API key created at the parent organization level. Use `group_by[]=organization_id` to break out per-organization values.
---@field time_bucket_width? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaAnalyticsTimeBucketWidth|string Time-bucket granularity. When set, rows are returned per time bucket (one per bucket and dimension combination with usage) and each row's `starting_at` and `ending_at` are that bucket's bounds; the time bucket counts toward `limit`. `ending_at` is required when `time_bucket_width` is set, and with `time_bucket_width="1m"` the range may span at most 24 hours. When omitted, each row aggregates the requested range with `starting_at` and `ending_at` each rounded down to the hour.
---@field order? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaAnalyticsUsageCostSortOrder|string Sort direction of the `order_by` metric, or of the time buckets when `order_by` is `time` and `time_bucket_width` is set. Defaults to `desc`.
---@field exclude_deleted_users? boolean If true, omit rows whose `actor` is a `user_actor` with `deleted: true`. Requires `group_by[]=actor`. Rows for other actor types, and rows whose `actor` is null, are always kept. A page may contain fewer than `limit` rows; use `has_more` and `next_page` to paginate as usual.
---@field limit? number Number of rows per page (1-1000, default 20). `cost_type`/`token_type` fan-out rows (cost endpoint only) do not count toward this limit, so `data` can exceed it.
---@field page? string Opaque cursor from a previous response's `next_page` field.
---@field order_by? anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaAnalyticsFlatCostOrderBy|string Row order. A metric ranks rows by that metric in the `order` direction. `time` orders rows by time bucket in the `order` direction (newest first by default) and, within a bucket, by `amount`, highest first. `time` takes effect only with `time_bucket_width`; without it, `time` is the same as `amount`. Defaults to `amount`.
---@field group_by__? anthropic.beta_organizations.GetAnalyticsCostRequestGroupByList Dimensions to break cost out by (at most 5, not counting `cost_type` and `token_type`): one row per combination of their values with cost in the range (and per time bucket, when `time_bucket_width` is set), every combination returned across pages rather than a capped top set. `cost_type` and `token_type` do not count toward `limit`: `cost_type` returns one row per cost component (tokens, web search, code execution, and `session_usage`, Claude Managed Agents session time); `token_type` returns one row per token type, each with `cost_type: "tokens"`; combining both returns the per-token-type rows plus the web-search, code-execution and session-usage rows. When omitted, a single row aggregates the whole range.
---@field anthropicVersion? string The version of the Claude API you want to use. Read more about versioning and our version history [here](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/versioning).
