---@field ref? string|distilled.Null The branch to validate the tip of, or the full 40-character SHA of the commit to validate. When omitted, the branch a synchronization would read (usually the repository's default branch); if that is not the default branch, the report's `ref` says which branch was read. An empty string, a value longer than 255 characters, or one that contains `..` or a character other than ASCII letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `-`, `+`, and `/`, is a 400. Any other value that is not a 40-character SHA is read as a branch name; if the repository has no such branch, the response is a report with `valid: false`, not a 400.
---@field repository_url string The `https://` URL of a public repository on github.com that holds the marketplace. A URL longer than 2,048 characters, on any other host or scheme, with a port other than 443 or 80, with credentials in it, or that does not name exactly `owner/repo` (a trailing `.git` or `/` is accepted) is a 400. A private or missing repository is reported in the response, not refused.

