---Add Federation Rule Workspace
---
---**Requires an OAuth access token with the `org:admin` scope**, from `ant auth login --scope org:admin` or a workload identity federation rule; Admin API keys are not accepted. See [Manage WIF with the Admin API](/docs/en/manage-claude/wif-admin-api).
---
---Enable a federation rule for a workspace.
---
---Idempotent; re-enabling returns the existing enablement. The rule and
---workspace must both belong to your organization. Membership of the
---rule's target service account in this workspace is not checked at
---enablement: token exchange into this workspace is rejected unless the
---target is a member (it is implicitly a member of the default workspace).
---Archived rules are rejected with 400. OAuth callers may only manage rules
---whose `oauth_scope` is `workspace:developer` or `workspace:inference`;
---other scopes require a Console session.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/federation_rules/{federation_rule_id}/workspaces`
---@param input anthropic.beta_organizations.AddFederationRuleWorkspaceRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaFederationRuleWorkspace? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:add_federation_rule_workspace(input) end

---Add RBAC Group Member
---
---Add a User to an RBAC Group. Membership of groups provisioned by an identity provider (source type `"scim"`) cannot be modified via the API while an organization in the tenant uses SCIM provisioning.
---
---The RBAC Groups API is available to Claude Enterprise organizations only.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/rbac_groups/{rbac_group_id}/members`
---@param input anthropic.beta_organizations.AddRbacGroupMemberRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaRbacGroupMember? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:add_rbac_group_member(input) end

---Add a Telemetry Destination Workspace
---
---Add one workspace to a destination's workspace list.
---
---Under `include` the workspace's spans start going to the destination. Under `exclude` they stop. A list holds at most 1,000 workspaces.
---
---Adding a workspace that is already on the list changes nothing and returns the existing entry. An archived workspace that isn't on the list yet can't be added. A destination whose `workspaces.type` is `all` doesn't have a list, so the API returns 400. To change which workspaces such a destination covers, update its `workspaces`.
---
---See the [OpenTelemetry export guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/opentelemetry#choose-workspaces-for-a-destination) to learn more about choosing the workspaces of a destination.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/telemetry_destinations/{destination_id}/workspaces/{workspace_id}`
---@param input anthropic.beta_organizations.AddTelemetryDestinationWorkspaceRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaTelemetryDestinationWorkspace? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:add_telemetry_destination_workspace(input) end

---Add Workspace To Service Account
---
---**Requires an OAuth access token with the `org:admin` scope**, from `ant auth login --scope org:admin` or a workload identity federation rule; Admin API keys are not accepted. See [Manage WIF with the Admin API](/docs/en/manage-claude/wif-admin-api).
---
---Add a service account to a workspace with the given `workspace_role`.
---
---Mirror of `POST /workspaces/{workspace_id}/service_accounts`, addressed
---from the service-account side; both create the same membership. If the
---service account is already an explicit member of the workspace, its
---`workspace_role` is replaced with the value supplied here. Archived
---workspaces return 400. Archived service accounts cannot be added and are
---rejected.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/service_accounts/{service_account_id}/workspaces`
---@param input anthropic.beta_organizations.AddWorkspaceToServiceAccountRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaServiceAccountWorkspaceMember? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:add_workspace_to_service_account(input) end

---Approve Spend Limit Increase Request
---
---Approve a pending spend limit increase request.
---
---Writes a per-user spend limit at `amount` for the requester and
