---Set Workspace Rate Limits
---
---Set or clear rate-limit overrides for one rate-limit group in a workspace.
---
---Only the limiter types named in `limits` change: an integer `value` sets
---that type's override and `null` clears it. Types not named keep their
---current value. A value above the organization's own limit is stored, but
---the organization limit still applies, so the lower of the two is
---enforced.
---
---Returns the targeted group's entry with this request applied, in the shape
---`GET /v1/organizations/workspaces/{workspace_id}/rate_limits` returns.
---Changes take effect within about an hour.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/workspaces/{workspace_id}/rate_limits/{rate_limit_id}`
---@param input anthropic.beta_organizations.UpdateWorkspaceRateLimitsRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaWorkspaceRateLimit? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_workspace_rate_limits(input) end

---Validate External Key
---
---Validate an external key config against the customer's KMS.
---
---Anthropic performs an encrypt/decrypt roundtrip against the configured
---KMS key and waits up to 30 seconds for the result. The response status is
---`success` if the roundtrip succeeded, or `failure` with an error
---message if it failed or timed out.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/external_keys/{external_key_id}/validate`
---@param input anthropic.beta_organizations.ValidateExternalKeyRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaValidateExternalKeyResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:validate_external_key(input) end

---Validate Plugin Marketplace Archive
---
---Check whether a plugin marketplace, uploaded as a `.zip` of the marketplace
---directory, would synchronize into claude.ai, without connecting or storing it.
---
---To check a public GitHub repository instead, use Validate Plugin Marketplace Repository.
---
---The report says whether `marketplace.json` is well-formed, which plugins a
---synchronization would skip and why, and which plugins would synchronize only in
---part, with some files left out. An archive that cannot be read as a marketplace is reported, not refused: the response is a report with `valid: false`. Plugin sources outside the marketplace
---are fetched anonymously from GitHub, so a private one is reported as not found or as
---needing a GitHub sign-in; a source on any other host is not fetched here, and the
---report notes that it will be checked when the marketplace actually synchronizes.
---
---Nothing is recorded on the Compliance API activity feed.
---
---For a worked example, see [Validate marketplace content](/docs/en/manage-claude/plugins-api#validate-marketplace-content)
---in the Plugins API guide.
---
---**Accepted credentials:** an Admin API key with the `read:plugins` or `write:plugins` scope; `read:org_audit` and `read:compliance_org_data` do not grant it.
---
---Every request must include the beta header `anthropic-beta: ce-plugins-2026-09-01`. A request without it returns `404`, exactly as if the endpoint did not exist. The Plugins API is in beta and is available to Claude Enterprise organizations only. It is not available to Claude Platform (Claude Console) organizations, or to organizations with HIPAA readiness enabled.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/plugin_marketplaces/validate_archive`
---@param input anthropic.beta_organizations.ValidatePluginMarketplaceArchiveRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaPluginMarketplaceValidationReport? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:validate_plugin_marketplace_archive(input) end

---Validate Plugin Marketplace Repository
---
---Check whether a plugin marketplace held in a public GitHub repository would
---synchronize into claude.ai, without connecting or storing it.
---
---To check a `.zip` of the marketplace directory instead, use Validate Plugin Marketplace Archive.
---
---The report says whether `marketplace.json` is well-formed, which plugins a
---synchronization would skip and why, and which plugins would synchronize only in
---part, with some files left out. A repository that is missing, private, or has no such branch or commit is reported, not refused: the response is a report with `valid: false`. Plugin sources outside the marketplace
---are fetched anonymously from GitHub, so a private one is reported as not found or as
---needing a GitHub sign-in; a source on any other host is not fetched here, and the
---report notes that it will be checked when the marketplace actually synchronizes.
---
---Nothing is recorded on the Compliance API activity feed.
---
---For a worked example, see [Validate marketplace content](/docs/en/manage-claude/plugins-api#validate-marketplace-content)
---in the Plugins API guide.
---
---**Accepted credentials:** an Admin API key with the `read:plugins` or `write:plugins` scope; `read:org_audit` and `read:compliance_org_data` do not grant it.
---
---Every request must include the beta header `anthropic-beta: ce-plugins-2026-09-01`. A request without it returns `404`, exactly as if the endpoint did not exist. The Plugins API is in beta and is available to Claude Enterprise organizations only. It is not available to Claude Platform (Claude Console) organizations, or to organizations with HIPAA readiness enabled.
---
---`POST /v1/organizations/plugin_marketplaces/validate_repository`
---@param input anthropic.beta_organizations.ValidatePluginMarketplaceRepositoryRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_organizations.BetaPluginMarketplaceValidationReport? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:validate_plugin_marketplace_repository(input) end

